# Docker build context: an ALLOW-LIST, so a new file stays out of the image
# until someone decides it belongs there.
#
# The `*` must stay the first line; each `!` line re-includes one path the
# build reads. Without it the whole working tree, a config file holding a live
# paperless-ngx token included, is sent to the daemon. This and the Dockerfile's
# named COPY lines are two independent gates; both would have to be wrong.
#
# Every entry is required: `uv sync --locked` needs uv.lock, and pyproject.toml's
# `readme` and `license-files` keys need README.md and LICENSE.
#
# tests/test_deployment_config.py pins this list, because CI's image build
# still succeeds with extra files in the context.
*
!src/
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
